#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128801 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "82248f5b-84f1-5acf-ade8-4ed90a410cc3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12530" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_1=1\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_2=2\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_3=3\\,\\textrm{kg},$ and $m_4=3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ located at $x_1=-1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_2 = 1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_3 = 3\\,\\textrm{m},$ and $x_4 = 5 \\, \\textrm{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =1, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3, & \\,{x}_{4} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-1+2+9+15 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128802 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "adcc17f7-7acf-50fd-bb68-b9e6b0477fe3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12531" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/cea41dc5efa961e4d0e3ccf42db21113d3b7d1d2240f3edbcc4c1f0cab61ead1.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overline{x},$ of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+4+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-2+8+12 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{18}{9}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128803 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "0f13ad0c-9523-542d-a3bf-c562f09d6a88" :question/math-academy-id "e-12532" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/0e4802c6642fc0950358235f30fb8c994d26b912e557122af08b99277bb6192a.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $(x_1y_1),(x_2,y_2),\\ldots,(x_n,y_n)$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m},\\dfrac{M_x}{m}\\right),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i y_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\nm_1 = 3, \\qquad m_2 = 5, \\qquad m_3 = 1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\ny_1 = 3, \\qquad y_2 = 0, \\qquad y_3 = 3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+5+1 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3+5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9+0+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{12}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128804 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/id #uuid "ae5cebdd-4eb8-5eed-9b89-fffb153c844b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12533" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/440f58e3d5e652374689083ffa672f505888259a51e1c5ef2207d94410eb8cab.png)\n\n     \n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $10\\,\\rm{lb}$ and is $4\\,\\rm{ft}$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A.$\nThe length of the rod is $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,\\rm{ft}.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n9 - 4 = 5\\,\\rm{ft},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/dc2503e1ed1cd91a9f3876ec5735d5c375c36b9bcac6216659a29f5efa294ea0.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m \\cdot 5 = -5m\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $10 \\cdot 4 = 40\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40-5m & =0 \\\\ 5m & =40 \\\\ m & =8\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af761a85-e4c8-5b27-81e9-97aca3773e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126669} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d5582b-4fec-5a73-8df1-d30026074e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126670} {:answer/id #uuid "c2575e83-b836-5df6-95db-e86cf00f8200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126671} {:answer/id #uuid "5c71ca70-8238-51cf-95aa-7b2c9c35b4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126672} {:answer/id #uuid "6149a7cb-85e4-5806-8acf-fa93c8fd3d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{44}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c71ca70-8238-51cf-95aa-7b2c9c35b4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{46}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126672} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b287a49-db3e-5d25-8be1-15e012197093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "581d1406-8e22-5cce-a290-02e4c2d04cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-163082" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/4561f2a4671ae67720e44d334d8bf75525fd72aeee62994cfea70c300702c5b4.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =3, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+3+1+5 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5+5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2+9+5+30 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{46}{11}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4495b4ea-7349-5a19-854a-7c2d696b79e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309140} {:answer/id #uuid "48894fe0-a31d-51bc-960a-85a36cabf623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309141} {:answer/id #uuid "422bdef6-b0d3-5a64-ac28-8b6ad2036061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309142} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c099e6-0d88-5c98-bb7a-98817f0c0e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309143} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3b4645-50b1-52b9-9f25-66c282897eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4495b4ea-7349-5a19-854a-7c2d696b79e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309140} :answer-field/id #uuid "9982e3e3-1fed-5e56-8c39-fa3f5f649b6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c92a5eca-b72e-5e6e-95be-47a34117a2da" :question/math-academy-id "q-163185" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1.5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=4\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=2\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=1\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=2\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{3}=4\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{4}=3\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1.5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, & \\,{m}_{4} & =2, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4, & \\,{x}_{4} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+1.5\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3+3+16+6 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f811546f-bd8f-5dd4-a213-627aa91a4162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309147} {:answer/id #uuid "e2747af4-7cd1-5aaa-abd7-5dcac26f7c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309148} {:answer/id #uuid "da9e9411-7694-5d57-930b-6aa08100269b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309149} {:answer/id #uuid "f74cdbaf-fc73-532e-b4cc-272821ee2c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} {:answer/id #uuid "60840850-2293-5a8d-9e2c-1bc0501f2c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f811546f-bd8f-5dd4-a213-627aa91a4162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309147} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3ce42ba-382e-5cce-9913-d08430e3d55e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d5de849-8db4-5330-9f8f-b2d802a64b63" :question/math-academy-id "q-163187" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=4\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=1\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=1.5\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=3\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1.5+4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+1.5+12 \\\\  & =18.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $18.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8e7e784-a95b-527e-908e-111a7bc1af92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309154} {:answer/id #uuid "04eb5dbf-cd20-5442-870e-c12448d49851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309155} {:answer/id #uuid "482ea3d0-33e9-586b-8c23-49b74840a63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309156} {:answer/id #uuid "535d7f4b-5e22-520b-acda-878ec40d8147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309157} {:answer/id #uuid "173da55b-110a-523f-8dae-32620208a66d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "535d7f4b-5e22-520b-acda-878ec40d8147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309157} :answer-field/id #uuid "03176b14-54a7-5c76-9b3d-8b33bb9879a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "403f8db4-df11-5433-9d6b-c89966b6432c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163223" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/6a3454379845a4202407ec16df4dee2cf31d0c67260952dd9a1cb07d48f7b936.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1.5, & \\,{m}_{4} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+1.5\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3+4+6+6 \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f3700e-e0a8-5b7c-a6e9-5341716902d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309161} {:answer/id #uuid "b5027a93-273f-5ded-8481-be1d614b2480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309162} {:answer/id #uuid "889f891c-4ef6-599b-85c8-60abc5edc45e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309163} {:answer/id #uuid "99147cd8-3053-5f9b-874d-5580978a0cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309164} {:answer/id #uuid "99652059-85d4-56b7-97bf-216ad7078d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99147cd8-3053-5f9b-874d-5580978a0cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309164} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aca303d-7473-55b7-8bb3-2af60fa24a3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5389b3bd-f290-5e12-87df-d61e71a585cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-163226" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/87d972a7f84c99cea7228de62a0f953bb62eca289a545cf905d0e16773e6dc50.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =1, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3, & \\,{x}_{4} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-4+9+5 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de779e53-edac-5d79-975e-fcd656fa6b02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309168} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff774ea-90eb-505f-8851-91cb0c563bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309169} {:answer/id #uuid "dc38d6d8-66cf-555b-8f36-719a41089e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309170} {:answer/id #uuid "4b28f316-dca7-5ec1-b8a5-7b7be12b0b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309171} {:answer/id #uuid "bace82ec-a08e-5d97-b138-1ac9e9a58678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b28f316-dca7-5ec1-b8a5-7b7be12b0b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309171} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5df886-2c21-543a-8f64-c000ab32de3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a0dfdab-0a73-52b7-ba86-94b54fe4c53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163229" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/eafe8cd97ea7c0dde38251a5f614b6611c97cf8263c55dbd73716f8179e51e58.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2.5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, & \\,{m}_{4} & =1.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2.5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5+1.5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =5+6+5+9 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a7bbd08-d3fa-595e-800c-79534a9c74e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309175} {:answer/id #uuid "94495d0f-113a-5982-aaa1-889afd77323f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309176} {:answer/id #uuid "79ea19ab-dcf8-5de1-b08a-31b9650a8720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309177} {:answer/id #uuid "621c4f03-8fc0-572e-9cc6-a8edabb0138c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309178} {:answer/id #uuid "627e027a-743c-5174-af84-24d7bb237d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "627e027a-743c-5174-af84-24d7bb237d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309179} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef0bb935-e8da-5c35-bd8d-f23b92bdbfa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dea7cb11-e94a-5589-afd8-6a0286d30694" :question/math-academy-id "q-163248" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=6\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=1\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-2,$ ${x}_{2}=2.5,$ ${x}_{3}=1,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =6, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =1, & \\,{x}_{4} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+6+1+5 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 2.5+1\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+15+1+20 \\\\  & =30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{30}{15}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7da8a0c7-7196-5d23-a15b-e020b560e69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309182} {:answer/id #uuid "0ae31a33-c76d-5796-b850-58baacaab227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309183} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce0541a-d385-5253-b477-69c14002512a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309184} {:answer/id #uuid "e5801ff4-a13a-5e3e-8837-365cb96ece29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309185} {:answer/id #uuid "0274c3b5-fd65-565a-ad24-05a1b8797c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5801ff4-a13a-5e3e-8837-365cb96ece29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309185} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae0f3cd-030f-5d79-a238-f3e185f59fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d06c244a-0804-5d77-966b-56ff5941b06f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163251" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=2\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=4\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ ${x}_{3}=0.5,$ and ${x}_{4}=1.5,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =2, & \\,{m}_{4} & =4, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =4, & \\,{x}_{3} & =0.5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =5+1+2+4 \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 0.5+4\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & =5+4+1+6 \\\\  & =16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{16}{12}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "851cac12-982e-50e8-9788-2a000859bf91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309189} {:answer/id #uuid "a7432724-7d27-5d01-9e02-ddf486aca1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309190} {:answer/id #uuid "c0528160-b3d8-5036-b377-96668342dcc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309191} {:answer/id #uuid "3e49df17-57f2-5eb8-ae44-fc6b8031dc3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309192} {:answer/id #uuid "e426e25f-5cb7-55ad-afa7-0d3135f470c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e426e25f-5cb7-55ad-afa7-0d3135f470c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309193} :answer-field/id #uuid "5546ee8d-9939-557b-92f3-5f610240f682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "349a8392-b508-5af5-9c2a-95ec7cbe6f78" :question/math-academy-id "q-163262" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/dc16f02e1eb47605ae2f21c64fd0f5c2c2bde6526a22d3965da5fa991869524e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =7, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =7+4+1 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-7+8+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc1968e9-44b7-59b3-9bd3-e1ac7131a921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309196} {:answer/id #uuid "282b76da-d8e5-55a5-aac5-973e0aa034ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309197} {:answer/id #uuid "d814f6e4-08ab-5ece-a80f-c228e6aacee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309198} {:answer/id #uuid "17bf30f2-6a76-542e-85d7-e672149638de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309199} {:answer/id #uuid "e834928b-0632-5d33-a77a-66fcb84f8168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "282b76da-d8e5-55a5-aac5-973e0aa034ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309197} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0de721e-dfcf-5791-941e-825cf03f9cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b1a5ca7-9bfa-5080-b5aa-33e63e68a521" :question/math-academy-id "q-163265" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/e16f9309d74f81f419ed96e995750bcad21a2770f214c49ee537f22ca25aac2e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =3, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =-0.5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+3+4+5 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot (-0.5)+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-6-2+10 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{-4}{14}=-\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d92d281-ccf7-5ff7-9616-05da58dad866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309203} {:answer/id #uuid "3b59f070-5553-5d4e-a069-9d1fb5eb7eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309204} {:answer/id #uuid "c7678f6c-2b0e-5a68-81f8-0afaadbae74d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309205} {:answer/id #uuid "905526be-2318-5e50-aa09-4b9997e4628d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309206} {:answer/id #uuid "27ec6b6b-9a39-5437-9d6a-142b2539bb5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27ec6b6b-9a39-5437-9d6a-142b2539bb5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309207} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7589019-c054-5d94-8d8f-ad0b87c00c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46ba6274-3fb3-5494-8cf2-40289eb1d004" :question/math-academy-id "q-163269" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/df939119a0cb5b9a5fdafc5158ecd299e91477247d7d6e920e2e167921ba4bdd.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=1,\\,{m}_{3}=7.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=1,\\,{x}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+1+7 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+1+28 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{23}{10}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c09699a9-2daf-5420-813b-20f17608bcb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309210} {:answer/id #uuid "03218cf4-827b-5a1e-8e59-f4cbc40ed725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309211} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e0af3-65aa-5b12-8f0a-c9f23f76d025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309212} {:answer/id #uuid "630cd070-7add-55d9-af46-e9c5f4373caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309213} {:answer/id #uuid "84b56a9e-ed15-509c-8d96-7d3d9d6cf663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09699a9-2daf-5420-813b-20f17608bcb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309210} :answer-field/id #uuid "051f6b2b-56fc-520f-80c0-7777ab3daa3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0982dd6f-cd45-5da5-a485-8151218b8587" :question/math-academy-id "q-163270" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/5d66682c96a14fb37ea0eb2deb46190fbe651e013a05c16a95577423b49b0ab9.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=1,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=6.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-4,\\,{x}_{2}=-2,\\,{x}_{3}=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =1+3+6 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-4-6+18 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{8}{10}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ecc71e3-cb63-53a7-8784-a1df56cc0fb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309217} {:answer/id #uuid "7c02d07f-b9a2-590a-8636-7b4356f001f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309218} {:answer/id #uuid "777e4735-e2b2-5a93-bca2-73a2e03041cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309219} {:answer/id #uuid "d36e1303-030c-5c21-aa23-dd21041e849c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309220} {:answer/id #uuid "25d9595e-4c33-54ca-abe1-b7ff2be92f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "777e4735-e2b2-5a93-bca2-73a2e03041cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309219} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e6b0750-2f04-5644-9b6b-9b8f19f207fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88a62ebc-9526-525a-badc-d55d33a5fa05" :question/math-academy-id "q-163271" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/fa8065896ec5efdc71402581c78674e4681fd02df2f7b945b0a182ae271fedfc.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=6,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=2,\\,{x}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =6+2+4 \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-18+4+16 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{2}{12}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da2af8f1-6aec-59f9-9e7a-da7076fec528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309224} {:answer/id #uuid "94500576-b1f7-5216-8285-d5ecbd06af04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309225} {:answer/id #uuid "5459ccf6-aecb-5f8f-812d-ddef748a11b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309226} {:answer/id #uuid "aac7b468-bdbb-54a9-8d6a-658845cffdf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309227} {:answer/id #uuid "337c413f-07ba-5a16-9706-d530e66a0550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac7b468-bdbb-54a9-8d6a-658845cffdf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309227} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3463db-8436-5774-9126-4622b4ecd0b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eedfc815-4546-56aa-9cb7-6ee7b9d4611a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163273" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/df6c2234a0b62d04157db126350e9b71f861af34ab42769245e553a8e228cb2b.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=4,\\,{y}_{2}=2,\\,{y}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+3+1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8+6+2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{16}{6}=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da9faa1f-5cc9-591f-b3bb-705b2f9c1ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309231} {:answer/id #uuid "90ec524d-8311-5fab-8f18-9800880c2288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309232} {:answer/id #uuid "3147cbe1-f22f-5050-9d5d-2c0ace8a9135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309233} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5685dc-1889-5ab3-8142-d0e7b22bea9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309234} {:answer/id #uuid "bca38a90-8e59-5a46-9767-05b106807456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a5685dc-1889-5ab3-8142-d0e7b22bea9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309234} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4040e3-8350-548f-9e5f-98b284791773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c900d2eb-6484-5d59-9646-3135c16323c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163276" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/e55b3a19251f3470401c081b24a90e90674844ce47d617dffd68bf161e2b7199.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=3,\\,{m}_{4}=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=3,\\,{y}_{2}=5,\\,{y}_{3}=2,\\,{y}_{4}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+2+3+1 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3}+{m}_{4}{y}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6+10+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{26}{8}=\\frac{13}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1294238-b0cc-5a1d-972b-0b6abfa5d0e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126723} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cfc22e-75d2-5cb1-acdc-04c01405bd43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126724} {:answer/id #uuid "06fda4c4-3073-5e7a-af27-2425381cedb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126725} {:answer/id #uuid "1e761749-3f64-5266-916d-62085fdf5c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126726} {:answer/id #uuid "6ead26d4-7517-595c-804e-6e6a2590d429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e761749-3f64-5266-916d-62085fdf5c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126726} :answer-field/id #uuid "e063d297-fd8c-5e50-bffc-a1c1dda34fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c837a8e-f3db-50ec-96a6-565fd7d0b50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163796" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/16e40e931919d695fe867f128827bc5351e390bb712009bfba130d195f5f35a2.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $10\\,kg$ and $8kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $5\\,m,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $A,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/6df23f8b7fd4202667daa23b1dc110bb1d546516fd37a2abd208b9c1c84b79c4.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-10\\cdot d=-10d\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $8\\cdot 5=40\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40-10d & =0 \\\\ 10d & =40 \\\\ d & =4\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8546df09-7ac1-5d49-90a0-ad3d968847be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126729} {:answer/id #uuid "c13a915e-cc5a-51aa-b88f-1effb98464e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126730} {:answer/id #uuid "c51de018-ac34-548d-921a-9ed25e54bebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126731} {:answer/id #uuid "290f70fa-9f21-55c8-a9d2-9be9801c94bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126732} {:answer/id #uuid "345aa25e-2ca4-5467-befd-a8c3ebeec36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "345aa25e-2ca4-5467-befd-a8c3ebeec36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126733} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6bf9b21-23a6-59b7-8c28-fa03a626adcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0d6fe0c-2d8e-592e-808b-507c87fc4991" :question/math-academy-id "q-163797" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/f0ca128a0755c0419d03d119501210b4be8036ccc0148f21b0e3a3665def30d5.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $10\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $3\\,kg$ and is $4\\,m$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A.$\nThe length of the rod is $10\\,m$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,m.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n10-4=6\\,m,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/a68789963345d21ca403d22a5f97ee440b0c3baa36345b0161bc7f80a8e0d1e0.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m\\cdot 6=-6m\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $3\\cdot 4=12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-6m & =0 \\\\ 6m & =12 \\\\ m & =2\\,kg.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be5b0627-bf7e-5a07-9053-c832cc2e5a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309238} {:answer/id #uuid "cefaf9ba-7d38-529c-bdbd-825c73bb2b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309239} {:answer/id #uuid "686a4c5a-e510-5952-81cb-4558f85b8be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309240} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d5a419-88c1-5fd6-b6e3-b1f9cac36ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309241} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c6308-1e03-53d7-a410-0b45a2535726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cefaf9ba-7d38-529c-bdbd-825c73bb2b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309239} :answer-field/id #uuid "6025c73a-0b67-58d7-9bab-4e3984a7af53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bfbc2cfa-782c-593d-b6ed-7e319d5ccc9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163802" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/97045288ee8cefe694fe6e30d7153d2cc78eb2c73a254f366f443f7230312148.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $10\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $4\\,kg$ and is $6\\,m$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A.$\nThe length of the rod is $10\\,m$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $6\\,m.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n10-6=4\\,m,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/ec39adee65bb0219053a8802470534cf8b2588f95cc8338c5c4a392adac6d516.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m\\cdot 4=-4m\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $4\\cdot 6=24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24-4m & =0 \\\\ 4m & =24 \\\\ m & =6\\,kg.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e54b040-651f-5b72-9f63-fede4e7ca214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309245} {:answer/id #uuid "9e3f6751-7ef9-52f4-83ac-210d2e0f1348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.3\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309246} {:answer/id #uuid "86010cd5-581b-5a23-90c1-4ad63893a8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309247} {:answer/id #uuid "c0eeda1f-5303-5f80-b066-34abebfdca42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309248} {:answer/id #uuid "191c9c5f-b811-51a3-9a12-069cc2759f03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.8\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e54b040-651f-5b72-9f63-fede4e7ca214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,lb" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309245} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cbce05a-d0b3-54ec-9211-e55e4feaeb2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c95ea01-feae-5636-bd7f-4cd1ac42fa53" :question/math-academy-id "q-163803" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/1292177200af79b36b05111607a33d0057d417c3e2f432de8439defb44e8928e.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $12\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $A$ has mass $6\\,lb$ and is $4\\,yd$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $B.$\nThe length of the rod is $12\\,yd$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $4\\,yd.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is\n\n$$\n12-4=8\\,yd,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/97c638d214774f8517b2724aabf8c91a1cc6b543f1ae17c5ba632acbe1ec59ff.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-6\\cdot 4=-24\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $m\\cdot 8=8m\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24+8m & =0 \\\\ 8m & =24 \\\\ m & =3\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c21c738-0c32-5c7f-96f4-9d61b17864a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309252} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a0add5-2c72-55f1-96d6-b49c3ce59ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309253} {:answer/id #uuid "e1217eaf-454d-51ec-900a-cd8bb552d356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309254} {:answer/id #uuid "be2e7b92-763d-55e2-8652-e81b1daff7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309255} {:answer/id #uuid "ac057dbd-2dbe-5792-b76e-c2ee453206d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1217eaf-454d-51ec-900a-cd8bb552d356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309254} :answer-field/id #uuid "80ae087a-f25f-5af3-aa07-ecfc77074163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b5967cb-a959-5be0-9c19-f06b6c3ac38a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163831" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/088d73d81b8b1705f8ff329ff38b8cd289bd8ecbe48ffc4c0bd18c823635b418.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $8\\,kg$ and $4\\,kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $6\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/31dd97f05b7dde8459bf79efbebcac082571c49282aeb63f926b0c1c058923c8.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-8\\cdot {d}_{1}=-8{d}_{1}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $4\\cdot {d}_{2}=4{d}_{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n4{d}_{2}-8{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{2},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{1}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $6\\,m,$ we have\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=6\\,⟹\\,{d}_{1}=6-{d}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{d}_{2}-8(6-{d}_{2}) & =0 \\\\ 4{d}_{2}-48+8{d}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{d}_{2} & =48 \\\\ {d}_{2} & =4\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
